// Two calls, one grant, and the two halves of the fail-open report.
//
// `util.inside_once()` carries the resource argument from the report: `mk()`
// names an in-grant path the first time it runs and `/etc/passwd` the second.
// The C backend evaluates that argument once now, so the check admits the path
// the call actually reads, which is the in-grant file. Before the fix the check
// saw the first evaluation and the call read the second, so this program printed
// the contents of `/etc/passwd` and exited 0.
//
// `util.outside()` is the control: out of the grant on every evaluation. It is
// denied at runtime, and the denial names `util.kp` where it is written.
impl "util" caps(fs = ["__KELP_SCRATCH__/kelp_caps_double_eval/**"])

fun main() {
    print(util.inside_once())
    print(util.outside())
}
